diff --git a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
index feabdcde0..002963514 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
@@ -145,6 +145,16 @@ The [generated tool reference](../../../docs/agents/mcp-tools.md) lists every to
 - `clear_tool_body { "tool": string }`: Remove a tool's body (either frame); the holder cylinder is judged again, and a turning tool's holder goes unjudged (its operations say so).
 - A body file too detailed to import at full fidelity (#864) is refused by name by every body tool: a coarse holder would read smaller than the holder is. Simplify the model and import again.
 - **Thread-mill tools (#989)**: `add_tool { "catalog": "TM-0600-P125" }` adds a multi-form mill at 1.25 mm pitch; `add_tool { "catalog": "TMS-0600-P050-150" }` adds a single-form mill for 0.5 to 1.5 mm pitches. In a full `definition` (copy the shape from `get_job`), `kind` is `"thread_mill"` or `"thread_mill_single"`. `pitch` is the multi-form mill's fixed pitch or the single-form mill's maximum pitch; `pitch_min` is the single-form mill's positive minimum pitch (no greater than `pitch`; omit it for a multi-form mill). A single-form definition without the `pitch_min` key reads as a range of its one `pitch` (#3662); a stated 0 is refused. Lengths and pitches are in mm; `diameter` spans the tooth crests, `flute_len` is the cutting length, and `tip_angle` is the included form angle in degrees. Thread milling requires the 60-degree form. Use `list_tool_catalog` for the full catalog definitions.
+- **Tool components and assemblies (#3647; `component_tools.rs`, `assembly_tools.rs`, `component_library_tools.rs`)**: an ISO 13399 tool is a stack of components (an `adaptive` holder or adapter, a `tool_item` cutter body with insert seats, an `insert`, a `solid` tool). The document holds a component table; a tool's assembly names rows of it, and the tool's diameter, corner radius and holder body are derived from the stack. A component object is `{ "id", "name", "item", "geometry"? }`, the form a `.camproj` `components` row has (`item` is `{ "insert": { "code" } }`, `{ "solid": { "mcs", "tool" } }`, `{ "tool_item": { "mcs", "seats" } }` or `{ "adaptive": { "mcs", "csw" } }`). Copy one from a `list_tool_components` row's `component`. `library` (optional on the library-reading tools) is a `.camcomponents` file; the default is the user's component library (`CAMCRAFT_COMPONENTS`, else the platform data folder).
+- `list_tool_components { "kind"?: "insert" | "solid" | "tool_item" | "adaptive", "scope"?: "all" | "builtin" | "user" | "document", "compatible_with"?: string, "library"?: string }`: List the built-in components (read only, `builtin:` ids), the user library and the document table. Each row is `{ scope, kind, ports, component }`; a document row adds `sync_status` (`not_linked`, `up_to_date`, `update_available`, `missing_from_library`, or `unreadable` with the reason). `compatible_with` names a component (document, then user library, then built-ins) and keeps the rows that fit with it, each with `fits: [{ as, port }]`: `as: "parent"` means the named component mounts on this row's `port` (the holders that take an insert); `as: "child"` means this row mounts on the named component's `port`. Refused by name: an unknown kind, scope or `compatible_with` id, and an unreadable library file.
+- `get_tool_assembly { "tool": string, "library"?: string }`: A document tool's stack: `nodes` (each with `component`, `name`, `kind`, `ports`, `mount` `{ parent, port, z_rot_deg, projection_mm }` or `null` for the root, `frame` (its MCS in the tool frame, tip at the origin) and `sync_status`), `cutting` `{ diameter, corner_r }`, `gauge_len` (cutting tip to spindle gauge line, mm), `solid_tool`, `holder_body`, and `links` (the `set_tool_assembly` input). Refused by name: an unknown or non-tool name, a tool with no assembly, an assembly that no longer resolves.
+- `set_tool_assembly { "tool": string, "links": [{ "component": string, "mount"?: { "parent": integer, "port"?: string, "z_rot_deg"?: number, "projection_mm"?: number } }] | null }`: Set a tool's stack, root first (no `mount`: the root, on the spindle; `parent` is a node index; `projection_mm` is a solid tool's stickout from a shank bore). Runs `SetToolAssembly`: the derived record and holder body land in one undo step, and the tool's operations go stale. `null` clears the stack and keeps the records. Refused by name, changing nothing: an unknown or non-tool name, an unknown key, an empty `links`, a component the document does not hold, a fit failure (the property is named), a bad port, frame or stickout, a lathe-held tool, a body in the flutes, an operation the new numbers strand.
+- `upsert_tool_component { "component": object }`: Add a component to the document table, or replace the one of the same id (`UpsertDocumentComponent`). A replace derives every tool built from it again in the same undo step and keeps the row's library link. Returns `{ component, added, updated_tools }`. Refused by name: a malformed component, an unknown key, a stated `library_ref`, an edit that changes nothing, an edit one of its tools cannot take (component and tool named; nothing changes).
+- `delete_tool_component { "id": string }`: Delete an unused component from the document table (`DeleteDocumentComponent`, one undo step). Refused by name: an unknown id, a component an assembly still uses (the tools are named).
+- `sync_tool_component { "id": string, "library"?: string }`: Replace a document component with its library copy (the linked copy, else the library component of the same id; built-ins included) and record the link (`SyncDocumentComponent`, one undo step). Every tool built from it is derived again; a sync of the same content records the link only. Returns `{ component, updated_tools }`. Refused by name: an unknown id, a copy the library does not hold, a component already up to date, a copy one of its tools cannot take. A project open never applies a library copy: only this tool does.
+- `save_library_component { "id"?: string, "component"?: object, "library"?: string }`: Save a document component (by `id`) or a full `component` to the user library, replacing an entry of the same id. A file edit, not a document change: no undo step. Then `sync_tool_component` links the document row to it. Refused by name: both or neither of `id` and `component`, an id the document does not hold, a `builtin:` id, a stated `library_ref`.
+- `delete_library_component { "id": string, "library"?: string }`: Delete an entry from the user library (a file edit, no undo). Linked document rows then show `missing_from_library`. Refused by name: a `builtin:` id, an id the library does not hold.
+- In a live GUI session (`--mcp-port`), `save_library_component` and `delete_library_component` ask for file-write approval, and a stated `library` on the reading tools asks for file access approval.
 
 ### 5. Operations & Geometric Features (`tools.rs`, `pick.rs`, `area.rs`, `features.rs`, #180, #312)
 - `list_operation_types {}`: Inspect all supported operation types, parameter schemas, defaults, and compatible tool types.
diff --git a/crates/app/src/mcp/assembly_tools.rs b/crates/app/src/mcp/assembly_tools.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..edc5f7cb4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/app/src/mcp/assembly_tools.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+//! The MCP tool assembly tools (#3647): read a document tool's
+//! component stack as the resolver judges it, and set or clear the
+//! stack through the very undoable `SetToolAssembly` the GUI queues
+//! (one History step that lands the derived tool record and holder
+//! body).
+//!
+//! Provenance: our own tool surface over this repo's assembly commands
+//! (#3644) and the ISO 13399 stack resolver (#3643).
+
+use serde_json::{Map, Value, json};
+
+use super::component_library_tools::{full_library, kind_word, library_prop, status_json};
+use super::setup_tools::{cmd_err, obj};
+use super::tools::{Tool, req_str};
+use crate::commands::SetToolAssembly;
+use crate::model;
+use crate::project::{FrameDto, LinkDto, assembly_to_dto};
+use crate::schema::AssemblyLink;
+use crate::script::Env;
+use crate::tool_assembly as ta;
+use camcraft_tools::tool_assembly::{AssemblyNode, Mount, resolve};
+
+pub(super) const TOOLS: &[Tool] = &[
+    Tool {
+        name: "get_tool_assembly",
+        description: "Read a document tool's component assembly: each node (component id, name, kind, ports, its mount on the parent: parent index, port, z_rot_deg and the stickout projection_mm, its MCS frame in the tool frame, and its library sync status), the derived cutting diameter and corner radius, the gauge length from the cutting tip to the spindle gauge line, and links (the form set_tool_assembly takes). Refused by name: an unknown or non-tool name, a tool with no assembly, and an assembly that no longer resolves.",
+        schema: s_get,
+        run: get_tool_assembly,
+    },
+    Tool {
+        name: "set_tool_assembly",
+        description: "Set a document tool's component assembly, root first: links is [{component, mount?: {parent, port?, z_rot_deg?, projection_mm?}}] (no mount: the root, on the spindle; parent is a node index). The derived tool record (diameter, corner radius, or a solid tool's own record) and the holder body land in one undo step, and the tool's operations go stale. links null clears the assembly and keeps the tool's records. Refused by name: an unknown or non-tool name, an unknown key, an empty links, a component the document does not hold, a component that does not fit its parent (the property is named), a bad port, frame or stickout, a lathe-held tool, a body in the flutes, and a change that an operation of the tool cannot take.",
+        schema: s_set,
+        run: set_tool_assembly,
+    },
+];
+
+fn s_get() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({
+            "tool": { "type": "string", "description": "A document tool's name." },
+            "library": library_prop(),
+        }),
+        &["tool"],
+    )
+}
+
+fn s_set() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({
+            "tool": { "type": "string", "description": "A document tool's name." },
+            "links": { "type": ["array", "null"], "items": { "type": "object" }, "description": "The stack, root first; null clears it." },
+        }),
+        &["tool", "links"],
+    )
+}
+
+/// The document tool `name`, or the refusal by name.
+fn tool_entity(env: &Env, name: &str) -> Result<flecs_ecs::prelude::Entity, String> {
+    let e = model::find_by_name(&env.world, name).ok_or_else(|| format!("no tool named '{name}'"))?;
+    if !model::is_tool(&env.world, &e) {
+        return Err(format!("'{name}' is not a tool"));
+    }
+    Ok(e)
+}
+
+/// The assembly view of tool `name` (see `get_tool_assembly`).
+fn view(env: &Env, a: &Map<String, Value>, name: &str) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let entity = tool_entity(env, name)?;
+    let Some(stack) = ta::assembly_of(&env.world, &entity) else {
+        return Err(format!("tool '{name}' has no tool assembly - set_tool_assembly builds one"));
+    };
+    let table = ta::components(&env.world);
+    let mut rows = Vec::with_capacity(stack.0.len());
+    let mut nodes = Vec::with_capacity(stack.0.len());
+    for link in &stack.0 {
+        let Some(row) = table.iter().find(|r| r.component.id() == link.component) else {
+            return Err(format!("tool '{name}': the assembly names the component '{}', which the document does not hold", link.component));
+        };
+        nodes.push(AssemblyNode { component: row.component.clone(), geometry: row.geometry.clone(), mount: link.mount.clone() });
+        rows.push(row);
+    }
+    let r = resolve(&nodes).map_err(|e| format!("tool '{name}': assembly: {e}"))?;
+    // The library is read only when a node links to it.
+    let library = if rows.iter().any(|r| r.library_ref.is_some()) { full_library(a) } else { Ok(Vec::new()) };
+    let out: Vec<Value> = rows
+        .iter()
+        .zip(&stack.0)
+        .enumerate()
+        .map(|(i, (row, link))| {
+            json!({
+                "index": i,
+                "component": row.component.id(),
+                "name": row.component.name(),
+                "kind": kind_word(&row.component),
+                "ports": row.component.ports(),
+                "mount": link.mount.as_ref().map(|m| json!({
+                    "parent": m.parent, "port": m.port, "z_rot_deg": m.z_rot_deg, "projection_mm": m.projection_mm,
+                })),
+                "frame": r.frames.get(i).map(|f| FrameDto { origin: f.origin(), z: f.z(), x: f.x() }),
+                "sync_status": status_json(row, &library),
+            })
+        })
+        .collect();
+    Ok(json!({
+        "tool": name,
+        "nodes": out,
+        "cutting": { "diameter": r.cutting.diameter, "corner_r": r.cutting.corner_r },
+        "gauge_len": r.gauge_len,
+        "solid_tool": r.tool.is_some(),
+        "holder_body": r.body.is_some(),
+        "links": assembly_to_dto(&stack),
+    }))
+}
+
+fn get_tool_assembly(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    view(env, a, req_str(a, "tool")?)
+}
+
+fn set_tool_assembly(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let name = req_str(a, "tool")?;
+    tool_entity(env, name)?;
+    let links = match a.get("links") {
+        None => return Err("\"links\" is required: the stack, root first, or null to clear it".to_owned()),
+        Some(Value::Null) => {
+            let cmd = SetToolAssembly::clear(&env.world, name).map_err(cmd_err)?;
+            env.history.execute(&env.world, cmd);
+            return Ok(json!({ "tool": name, "assembly": Value::Null }));
+        }
+        Some(v @ Value::Array(_)) => {
+            serde_json::from_value::<Vec<LinkDto>>(v.clone()).map_err(|e| format!("bad \"links\": {e}"))?
+        }
+        Some(other) => return Err(format!("\"links\" must be an array or null, got {other}")),
+    };
+    if links.is_empty() {
+        return Err("\"links\" is empty - give null to clear the assembly".to_owned());
+    }
+    let links: Vec<AssemblyLink> = links
+        .into_iter()
+        .map(|l| AssemblyLink {
+            component: l.component,
+            mount: l.mount.map(|m| Mount { parent: m.parent, port: m.port, z_rot_deg: m.z_rot_deg, projection_mm: m.projection_mm }),
+        })
+        .collect();
+    let cmd = SetToolAssembly::new(&env.world, name, links).map_err(cmd_err)?;
+    env.history.execute(&env.world, cmd);
+    view(env, a, name)
+}
diff --git a/crates/app/src/mcp/component_library_tools.rs b/crates/app/src/mcp/component_library_tools.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..cdab82658
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/app/src/mcp/component_library_tools.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
+//! The MCP user component library tools (#3647): save a tool component
+//! to the user's component library, delete one from it, and the shared
+//! readers the component and assembly tools use (the library file, the
+//! sync status, a row's JSON). A save and a delete are file edits, not
+//! document commands (`component_library::store`): no undo step, and a
+//! `builtin:` id is refused by name.
+//!
+//! Provenance: our own tool surface over this repo's component library
+//! store (#3645).
+
+use std::path::PathBuf;
+
+use serde_json::{Map, Value, json};
+
+use super::setup_tools::obj;
+use super::tools::{Tool, opt_str, req_str};
+use crate::component_library::{self, LibraryComponent, SyncStatus, store};
+use crate::project::{ComponentDto, component_from_dto, component_to_dto};
+use crate::schema::DocumentComponent;
+use crate::script::Env;
+use crate::tool_assembly as ta;
+use camcraft_tools::component::{ComponentKind, CuttingItem, ToolComponent};
+
+pub(super) const TOOLS: &[Tool] = &[
+    Tool {
+        name: "save_library_component",
+        description: "Save a tool component to the user's component library: a document component by id, or a full component (the component object of a list_tool_components row). An entry with the same id is replaced. A file edit, not a document change: no undo step. Refused by name: both or neither of id and component, an id the document does not hold, a builtin: id (built-in components are read only), a component that states library_ref, and every component check.",
+        schema: s_save,
+        run: save_library_component,
+    },
+    Tool {
+        name: "delete_library_component",
+        description: "Delete a tool component from the user's component library. A file edit, not a document change: no undo step. Document components linked to it then show the sync status missing_from_library. Refused by name: a builtin: id (built-in components are read only) and an id the library does not hold.",
+        schema: s_delete,
+        run: delete_library_component,
+    },
+];
+
+/// The schema row of the optional `library` argument.
+pub(super) fn library_prop() -> Value {
+    json!({ "type": "string", "description": "A component library file (.camcomponents). Default: the user's component library (CAMCRAFT_COMPONENTS, else the platform data folder)." })
+}
+
+fn s_save() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({
+            "id": { "type": "string", "description": "A document component's id: save that component." },
+            "component": { "type": "object", "description": "A full component: {id, name, item, geometry?} as list_tool_components shows it, without library_ref." },
+            "library": library_prop(),
+        }),
+        &[],
+    )
+}
+
+fn s_delete() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({
+            "id": { "type": "string", "description": "The library component's id." },
+            "library": library_prop(),
+        }),
+        &["id"],
+    )
+}
+
+/// The library file: `library` when given, else the user's own.
+pub(super) fn library_path(a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<PathBuf, String> {
+    match opt_str(a, "library")? {
+        Some(p) if !p.trim().is_empty() => Ok(PathBuf::from(p)),
+        _ => store::user_dir()
+            .map(|d| store::library_path(&d))
+            .ok_or_else(|| format!("no user folder for the component library - set {}", store::ENV_VAR)),
+    }
+}
+
+/// The user's components (not the built-ins). A refused file is an
+/// error, never "empty".
+pub(super) fn user_library(a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Vec<LibraryComponent>, String> {
+    store::load(&library_path(a)?)
+}
+
+/// The library a document syncs from: the built-ins, then the user's.
+pub(super) fn full_library(a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Vec<LibraryComponent>, String> {
+    user_library(a).map(component_library::with_builtins)
+}
+
+/// The kind word of a component, as `list_tool_components` filters it.
+pub(super) fn kind_word(c: &ToolComponent) -> &'static str {
+    match c.kind() {
+        ComponentKind::CuttingItem(CuttingItem::Insert(_)) => "insert",
+        ComponentKind::CuttingItem(CuttingItem::Solid { .. }) => "solid",
+        ComponentKind::ToolItem { .. } => "tool_item",
+        ComponentKind::AdaptiveItem { .. } => "adaptive",
+    }
+}
+
+/// The sync status of a document row. A row with no link needs no
+/// library; an unreadable library is said, never read as "missing".
+pub(super) fn status_json(row: &DocumentComponent, library: &Result<Vec<LibraryComponent>, String>) -> Value {
+    let Some(link) = &row.library_ref else {
+        return json!({ "status": "not_linked" });
+    };
+    let lib = match library {
+        Ok(l) => l,
+        Err(e) => return json!({ "status": "unreadable", "library_id": link.id, "reason": e }),
+    };
+    match component_library::sync_status(row, lib) {
+        SyncStatus::NotLinked => json!({ "status": "not_linked" }),
+        SyncStatus::UpToDate => json!({ "status": "up_to_date", "library_id": link.id }),
+        SyncStatus::UpdateAvailable { library_hash } => {
+            json!({ "status": "update_available", "library_id": link.id, "library_hash": library_hash })
+        }
+        SyncStatus::MissingFromLibrary => json!({ "status": "missing_from_library", "library_id": link.id }),
+    }
+}
+
+/// One listed row: where it lives, its kind and ports, and the wire
+/// form under `component` (the form `upsert_tool_component` takes).
+pub(super) fn row_json(scope: &str, dto: &ComponentDto, c: &ToolComponent) -> Value {
+    json!({ "scope": scope, "kind": kind_word(c), "ports": c.ports(), "component": dto })
+}
+
+/// The wire form of a library entry.
+pub(super) fn library_dto(e: &LibraryComponent) -> ComponentDto {
+    component_to_dto(&DocumentComponent { component: e.component.clone(), geometry: e.geometry.clone(), library_ref: None })
+}
+
+/// The checked component under `key`. A stated `library_ref` is
+/// refused: only `sync_tool_component` writes a library link.
+pub(super) fn parse_component(a: &Map<String, Value>, key: &str) -> Result<DocumentComponent, String> {
+    let v = match a.get(key) {
+        Some(v @ Value::Object(_)) => v.clone(),
+        None | Some(Value::Null) => return Err(format!("\"{key}\" is required")),
+        Some(other) => return Err(format!("\"{key}\" must be an object, got {other}")),
+    };
+    let dto: ComponentDto = serde_json::from_value(v).map_err(|e| format!("bad \"{key}\": {e}"))?;
+    if dto.library_ref.is_some() {
+        return Err(format!(
+            "\"{key}\" states library_ref - only sync_tool_component writes a library link"
+        ));
+    }
+    component_from_dto(&dto)
+}
+
+fn save_library_component(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let row = match (opt_str(a, "id")?, a.get("component").filter(|v| !v.is_null())) {
+        (Some(_), Some(_)) => return Err("give id or component, not both".to_owned()),
+        (None, None) => return Err("give id (a document component) or component (a full component)".to_owned()),
+        (Some(id), None) => ta::component(&env.world, id)
+            .ok_or_else(|| format!("the document holds no tool component '{}'", id.trim()))?,
+        (None, Some(_)) => parse_component(a, "component")?,
+    };
+    let id = row.component.id().to_owned();
+    if component_library::is_builtin_id(&id) {
+        return Err(format!("tool component '{id}' is built in - it is not saved to the user library"));
+    }
+    let entry = LibraryComponent { component: row.component, geometry: row.geometry };
+    let content_hash = entry.content_hash();
+    let path = library_path(a)?;
+    store::put(&path, entry)?;
+    Ok(json!({ "saved": id, "content_hash": content_hash, "library": path.display().to_string() }))
+}
+
+fn delete_library_component(_env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let id = req_str(a, "id")?.trim();
+    let path = library_path(a)?;
+    store::delete(&path, id)?;
+    Ok(json!({ "deleted": id, "library": path.display().to_string() }))
+}
diff --git a/crates/app/src/mcp/component_tools.rs b/crates/app/src/mcp/component_tools.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..edf6c602f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/app/src/mcp/component_tools.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,215 @@
+//! The MCP document tool component tools (#3647): list the built-in,
+//! user-library and document components (with a compatibility query),
+//! and add, edit, delete and sync a document component. Each write runs
+//! the very undoable command the GUI queues (`UpsertDocumentComponent`,
+//! `DeleteDocumentComponent`, `SyncDocumentComponent`): one History
+//! step, and every tool built from an edited component is derived again
+//! in that step.
+//!
+//! Provenance: our own tool surface over this repo's component commands
+//! (#3644), component library (#3645) and ISO 13399 fit checks (#3643).
+
+use serde_json::{Map, Value, json};
+
+use super::component_library_tools::{
+    full_library, kind_word, library_dto, library_path, library_prop, parse_component, row_json, status_json,
+    user_library,
+};
+use super::setup_tools::{cmd_err, obj};
+use super::tools::{Tool, opt_str, req_str};
+use crate::commands::{DeleteDocumentComponent, SyncDocumentComponent, UpsertDocumentComponent};
+use crate::component_library;
+use crate::project::component_to_dto;
+use crate::script::Env;
+use crate::tool_assembly as ta;
+use camcraft_tools::component::ToolComponent;
+use camcraft_tools::component_fit::{compatible_children, compatible_parents};
+
+pub(super) const TOOLS: &[Tool] = &[
+    Tool {
+        name: "list_tool_components",
+        description: "List tool components: the built-in ones (read only, builtin: ids), the user's component library and the document's component table. Each row has scope (builtin, user or document), kind (insert, solid, tool_item or adaptive), ports and the component itself (the form upsert_tool_component takes); a document row also has its library sync status. kind and scope filter the rows. compatible_with names a component (looked up in the document, then the user library, then the built-ins) and keeps only the rows that fit with it, each with fits: [{as: parent | child, port}] (as parent: the named component mounts on this row's port; as child: this row mounts on the named component's port). Refused by name: an unknown kind or scope, an unknown compatible_with id, and an unreadable library file.",
+        schema: s_list,
+        run: list_tool_components,
+    },
+    Tool {
+        name: "upsert_tool_component",
+        description: "Add a tool component to the document's component table, or replace the component of the same id. A replace derives every tool whose assembly uses the component again (diameter, corner radius, holder body) in the same undo step, and keeps the row's library link. One undo step. Refused by name: a malformed component, an unknown key, a component that states library_ref (use sync_tool_component), an edit that changes nothing, and an edit that a tool built from it cannot take (the tool is named; nothing changes).",
+        schema: s_upsert,
+        run: upsert_tool_component,
+    },
+    Tool {
+        name: "delete_tool_component",
+        description: "Delete a component from the document's component table. One undo step. Refused by name: an id the document does not hold, and a component that a tool assembly still uses (the tools are named).",
+        schema: s_id,
+        run: delete_tool_component,
+    },
+    Tool {
+        name: "sync_tool_component",
+        description: "Replace a document component with its library copy (the copy it links to, or the library component of the same id) and record the link. Every tool built from it is derived again in the same undo step. One undo step. Refused by name: an id the document does not hold, a copy the library does not hold, a component already up to date, and a copy that a tool built from it cannot take.",
+        schema: s_sync,
+        run: sync_tool_component,
+    },
+];
+
+/// Every component, assembly and component library row (#3647).
+pub(super) fn all() -> impl Iterator<Item = &'static Tool> {
+    TOOLS.iter().chain(super::assembly_tools::TOOLS).chain(super::component_library_tools::TOOLS)
+}
+
+const KINDS: &[&str] = &["insert", "solid", "tool_item", "adaptive"];
+const SCOPES: &[&str] = &["all", "builtin", "user", "document"];
+
+fn s_list() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({
+            "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": KINDS, "description": "Only components of this kind." },
+            "scope": { "type": "string", "enum": SCOPES, "description": "Only components from here (default all)." },
+            "compatible_with": { "type": "string", "description": "A component id: only the components that fit with it." },
+            "library": library_prop(),
+        }),
+        &[],
+    )
+}
+
+fn s_upsert() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({ "component": { "type": "object", "description": "The component: {id, name, item, geometry?} (the component object of a list_tool_components row)." } }),
+        &["component"],
+    )
+}
+
+fn s_id() -> Value {
+    obj(json!({ "id": { "type": "string", "description": "The document component's id." } }), &["id"])
+}
+
+fn s_sync() -> Value {
+    obj(
+        json!({
+            "id": { "type": "string", "description": "The document component's id." },
+            "library": library_prop(),
+        }),
+        &["id"],
+    )
+}
+
+/// One candidate row: its scope, the component, and the listed JSON
+/// without the fit (added when `compatible_with` is given).
+struct Row {
+    scope: &'static str,
+    component: ToolComponent,
+    json: Value,
+}
+
+fn word<'a>(a: &'a Map<String, Value>, key: &str, words: &[&str]) -> Result<Option<&'a str>, String> {
+    match opt_str(a, key)? {
+        None => Ok(None),
+        Some(w) if words.contains(&w) => Ok(Some(w)),
+        Some(w) => Err(format!("unknown {key} '{w}' - one of {}", words.join(", "))),
+    }
+}
+
+fn list_tool_components(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let kind = word(a, "kind", KINDS)?;
+    let scope = word(a, "scope", SCOPES)?.unwrap_or("all");
+    let wants = |s: &str| scope == "all" || scope == s;
+    let target_id = opt_str(a, "compatible_with")?.map(str::trim);
+    let table = ta::components(&env.world);
+    // The user library is read when its rows are listed, or when a
+    // compatibility query names a component the document does not hold.
+    let in_doc = target_id.is_some_and(|id| table.iter().any(|r| r.component.id() == id));
+    let user = if wants("user") || (target_id.is_some() && !in_doc) { Some(user_library(a)?) } else { None };
+    let sync_lib = match &user {
+        Some(u) => Ok(component_library::with_builtins(u.clone())),
+        None if table.iter().any(|r| r.library_ref.is_some()) => full_library(a),
+        None => Ok(Vec::new()),
+    };
+
+    let mut rows = Vec::new();
+    for r in table {
+        let mut json = row_json("document", &component_to_dto(&r), &r.component);
+        json["sync_status"] = status_json(&r, &sync_lib);
+        rows.push(Row { scope: "document", component: r.component, json });
+    }
+    for e in user.iter().flatten() {
+        rows.push(Row { scope: "user", json: row_json("user", &library_dto(e), &e.component), component: e.component.clone() });
+    }
+    for e in component_library::builtins() {
+        rows.push(Row { scope: "builtin", json: row_json("builtin", &library_dto(&e), &e.component), component: e.component });
+    }
+
+    let target = match target_id {
+        None => None,
+        Some(id) => Some(
+            rows.iter()
+                .find(|r| r.component.id() == id)
+                .map(|r| (r.scope, r.component.clone()))
+                .ok_or_else(|| format!("no tool component '{id}' in the document or the component library"))?,
+        ),
+    };
+
+    let mut out = Vec::new();
+    for mut r in rows {
+        if !wants(r.scope) || kind.is_some_and(|k| kind_word(&r.component) != k) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if let Some((_, t)) = &target {
+            let mut fits: Vec<Value> = compatible_parents(t, [&r.component])
+                .into_iter()
+                .map(|f| json!({ "as": "parent", "port": f.port }))
+                .collect();
+            fits.extend(compatible_children(t, [&r.component]).into_iter().map(|f| json!({ "as": "child", "port": f.port })));
+            if fits.is_empty() {
+                continue;
+            }
+            r.json["fits"] = Value::Array(fits);
+        }
+        out.push(r.json);
+    }
+    let library = library_path(a).ok().map(|p| p.display().to_string());
+    Ok(json!({
+        "count": out.len(),
+        "components": out,
+        "compatible_with": target.map(|(s, c)| json!({ "id": c.id(), "scope": s })),
+        "library": library,
+    }))
+}
+
+/// The document row `id` as a listed row, with its sync status.
+fn document_row(env: &Env, a: &Map<String, Value>, id: &str) -> Value {
+    match ta::component(&env.world, id) {
+        Some(r) => {
+            let mut json = row_json("document", &component_to_dto(&r), &r.component);
+            let library = if r.library_ref.is_some() { full_library(a) } else { Ok(Vec::new()) };
+            json["sync_status"] = status_json(&r, &library);
+            json
+        }
+        None => Value::Null,
+    }
+}
+
+fn upsert_tool_component(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let row = parse_component(a, "component")?;
+    let id = row.component.id().to_owned();
+    let added = ta::component(&env.world, &id).is_none();
+    let cmd = UpsertDocumentComponent::new(&env.world, row.component, row.geometry).map_err(cmd_err)?;
+    let updated = cmd.updated_tools();
+    env.history.execute(&env.world, cmd);
+    Ok(json!({ "component": document_row(env, a, &id), "added": added, "updated_tools": updated }))
+}
+
+fn delete_tool_component(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let id = req_str(a, "id")?.trim();
+    let cmd = DeleteDocumentComponent::new(&env.world, id).map_err(cmd_err)?;
+    env.history.execute(&env.world, cmd);
+    Ok(json!({ "deleted": id }))
+}
+
+fn sync_tool_component(env: &mut Env, a: &Map<String, Value>) -> Result<Value, String> {
+    let id = req_str(a, "id")?.trim();
+    let library = full_library(a)?;
+    let cmd = SyncDocumentComponent::new(&env.world, id, &library).map_err(cmd_err)?;
+    let updated = cmd.updated_tools();
+    env.history.execute(&env.world, cmd);
+    Ok(json!({ "component": document_row(env, a, id), "updated_tools": updated }))
+}
